# Fix Serverless Function Crash on Vercel

The API (`/api/*`) crashes on Vercel because any uncaught exception during module initialization (i.e. during `import app from '../backend/src/server'`) kills the entire serverless function before it can respond. There is no try-catch boundary at the entry point, and several modules perform side-effects at import time that can throw.

## Root Causes Found

| # | Root Cause | File | Severity |
|---|-----------|------|----------|
| 1 | **No error boundary at entry point** — any import-time crash = 500 | [api/index.ts](file:///d:/HOPPER/VINHPART_PROJECT/api/index.ts) | 🔴 Critical |
| 2 | **`dotenv.config()` called AFTER route imports** — `DATABASE_URL`, `CLOUDINARY_*` are `undefined` when [database.ts](file:///d:/HOPPER/VINHPART_PROJECT/backend/src/shared/database.ts) and [cloudinary.ts](file:///d:/HOPPER/VINHPART_PROJECT/backend/src/shared/cloudinary.ts) modules initialize | [server.ts](file:///d:/HOPPER/VINHPART_PROJECT/backend/src/server.ts) L19 vs L1-17 | 🔴 Critical |
| 3 | **`import.meta.url` / `fileURLToPath`** — can fail in Vercel's esbuild bundler | [server.ts](file:///d:/HOPPER/VINHPART_PROJECT/backend/src/server.ts) L4-5, L21-22 | 🟡 Medium |
| 4 | **`new Pool()` with bad connection string** — `DATABASE_URL` is empty → pool errors on cold start | [database.ts](file:///d:/HOPPER/VINHPART_PROJECT/backend/src/shared/database.ts) | 🟡 Medium |
| 5 | **`cloudinary.config()` with `undefined` keys** — silently misconfigures → may throw in some versions | [cloudinary.ts](file:///d:/HOPPER/VINHPART_PROJECT/backend/src/shared/cloudinary.ts) | 🟢 Low |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Root cause #2 is likely the #1 offender. On Vercel, environment variables are set via the dashboard (not [.env](file:///d:/HOPPER/VINHPART_PROJECT/.env) file), so `dotenv.config()` is a no-op there. But the [database.ts](file:///d:/HOPPER/VINHPART_PROJECT/backend/src/shared/database.ts) module reads `process.env.DATABASE_URL` at the top level. If Vercel env vars aren't set correctly, `connectionString` becomes empty and `new Pool()` gets a bad config. Combined with root cause #1 (no error boundary), any resulting exception crashes the function immediately.

## Proposed Changes

### API Entry Point

#### [MODIFY] [index.ts](file:///d:/HOPPER/VINHPART_PROJECT/api/index.ts)

Wrap the entire export in a try-catch error boundary. If the server module fails to import, return a diagnostic JSON response instead of crashing the function.

```diff
-import app from '../backend/src/server';
-
-export default app;
+import type { VercelRequest, VercelResponse } from '@vercel/node';
+
+let app: any;
+let initError: Error | null = null;
+
+try {
+    const serverModule = await import('../backend/src/server.js');
+    app = serverModule.default;
+} catch (err) {
+    initError = err instanceof Error ? err : new Error(String(err));
+    console.error('❌ Failed to initialize server module:', initError);
+}
+
+export default function handler(req: VercelRequest, res: VercelResponse) {
+    if (initError || !app) {
+        res.status(503).json({
+            error: 'Server initialization failed',
+            message: initError?.message || 'Unknown error',
+            stack: process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production' ? initError?.stack : undefined,
+        });
+        return;
+    }
+    return app(req, res);
+}
```

---

### Backend Server

#### [MODIFY] [server.ts](file:///d:/HOPPER/VINHPART_PROJECT/backend/src/server.ts)

1. Move `dotenv.config()` to the very top, before any imports that depend on env vars.
2. Remove `import.meta.url` / `fileURLToPath` usage — unnecessary for Vercel deployment and error-prone. Use `process.cwd()` as fallback.
3. Add defensive `try-catch` around static file serving setup.

---

### Shared Database Module

#### [MODIFY] [database.ts](file:///d:/HOPPER/VINHPART_PROJECT/backend/src/shared/database.ts)

Add defensive check for missing `DATABASE_URL` and log a warning, so the pool is still created (with empty connection string) but the error is visible in logs.

---

### Shared Cloudinary Module

#### [MODIFY] [cloudinary.ts](file:///d:/HOPPER/VINHPART_PROJECT/backend/src/shared/cloudinary.ts)

Wrap `cloudinary.config()` call in a `try-catch` with warning log.

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- No existing test suite found in the project.
- Run TypeScript type-check: `npx tsc --noEmit` from project root to verify no type errors.

### Manual Verification
1. Run `npm run dev:server` from project root and verify the server starts without crashing.
2. After deploying to Vercel, if the server module fails to initialize, the API should return a `503` JSON response with the error message instead of a raw crash — this lets you see the actual error in the response body and Vercel function logs.
3. User should verify Vercel environment variables are correctly configured (`DATABASE_URL`, `CLOUDINARY_*`, etc.) via the Vercel dashboard.

> [!TIP]
> After deploying the fix, test by hitting any API endpoint (e.g. `GET /api/products`). If it returns data → fixed. If it returns a `503` JSON → the error message will tell you exactly what's still wrong.
